title: RevStealer Fake Claude Opus 5 - Suspicious Electron App Execution
id: e1c7f5a8-36d0-7b2e-f9c5-7a1d3e6b2c8f
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects execution patterns of the fake Claude Opus 5 application that
    deploys RevStealer, a Windows information stealer (gbhackers, 2026).
    The ~101 MB Electron executable performs anti-analysis checks including
    physical memory inspection, CPU core count, hostname/username queries,
    and debugger timing checks before decrypting an AES-256-CBC payload.
    The malware steals browser data, password managers, crypto wallets,
    VPN sessions, and Windows Credential Manager contents.
references:
    - https://gbhackers.com
    - https://cyberpress.org
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/09/02
tags:
    - attack.t1036
    - attack.t1204
    - attack.t1539
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_electron:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\electron.exe'
            - '\Claude Opus 5.exe'
            - '\claude.exe'
    selection_suspicious_parent:
        ParentImage|contains:
            - '\AppData\Local\Temp\'
            - '\Downloads\'
            - '\Desktop\'
    selection_suspicious_cmd:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'Claude'
            - 'Opus'
            - 'Anthropic'
    condition: selection_electron and (selection_suspicious_parent or selection_suspicious_cmd)
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate Electron applications installed by the user
level: medium
